does this scream sound familiar that's  because it's used in over 100 films it's  a movie trope called the Wilhelm scream  the Wilhelm scream is maybe the most  famous sound effect in Hollywood it is  used when characters are shot or fall  off high places in action films the  scream made its first appearance in a  1951 film called distant drums and  there's a moment in the film where a  character is dragged into the swamp and  they wanted a particularly  blood-curdling scream now this was just  one of many different screams in the  film to make a film you need a sound  effects library a collection of sound  effects and you're going to use them in  different parts of the film maybe in one  part of your action film you need a  two-second scream but in another part of  your film you might need a one and a  half second blood-curdling screams  producers had cast members record a  variety of different screams but there  was one man scream a particular that  stood out among the rest it's usually  credited now to Sheb Wooley who was a  kind of a western style character actor  and a novelty singer who appears in  distant drums but its first appearance  in 1951 wasn't the screams shining  moment that happened when it was used  again in the 1953 film the charge at  Feather River a character named private  Wilhelm was shot in the leg with an  arrow  and that's how it got named the Wilhelm  scream since then the sound has been  used in more than 100 films  [Music]  why well for one it's cheaper and easier  to reuse pre-existing sound effects you  have to give credit to Ben Burtt the  wonderful sound designer who's been  working on the biggest films in  Hollywood since the 1970s close  associate of George Lucas he's the one  who really discovered the Wilhelm scream  and researched out its origins Burtt  used the scream in a memorable moment in  Star Wars Luke Skywalker fires at a  stormtrooper this cream actually appears  in all of the original Star Wars films  and then it became an in-joke the screen  then spread to many other famous films  Steven Spielberg picked up on it used it  many many of his films and then it just  went crazy of course Peter Jackson uses  it in the Lord of the Rings even shows  up in Toy Story and Reservoir Dogs the  sound is now famous among film buffs I  think you can go on YouTube and see  compilations of dozens of Willhelm  screams I mean it has its own Wikipedia  entry and so for people that love movies  this is part of their enjoyment of it is  finding this little insider detail  [Music]
 

